WEBVTT

00:08:28.829 --> 00:08:30.329
And obviously, I think that's a problem.

00:08:30.954 --> 00:08:36.246
And I think that maybe the first way to
get people past that fear is we need

00:08:36.246 --> 00:08:38.829
people in positions of power
to model it. Right.

00:08:38.829 --> 00:08:42.662
We know that if you've been validated
by your power or your status

00:08:42.662 --> 00:08:46.871
or your authority, that people are much
more comfortable letting you say you

00:08:46.871 --> 00:08:49.996
don't know. There's evidence, for example,
that when experts say,

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:53.371
I'm not sure or I don't know, they
actually become more persuasive,

00:08:54.162 --> 00:08:57.246
in part because we respect their
humility and in part

00:08:57.246 --> 00:08:59.829
because we're surprised that we
actually pay more attention to

00:08:59.829 --> 00:09:02.121
the substance of their argument, which,
you know,